From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:13:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Distribute spanning items' leftover space to non-affected
 tracks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

css-grid-2 §12.5.1 gained a step between "distribute space up to limits"
and "distribute space beyond limits" (w3c/csswg-drafts#3648): when the
affected tracks have all reached their limits and the item also spans
other tracks, the remaining space goes into those other tracks, up to
their own limits, before any affected track grows past its growth limit.

Without it, `min-content minmax(max-content, 30px)` with one item
spanning both columns put the item's max-content overflow into the
capped second column (20px 70px) instead of the first (60px 30px), and a
1px min-content overflow went to a column whose growth limit an empty
item had already pinned at zero. WPT ed5a113c rebaselined
css-grid/parsing/grid-content-sized-columns-resolution.html and
css-grid/grid-model/grid-gutters-and-flex-content-001.html for this
(WebKit 322402@main).

Upstream Taffy (main) does not have this step either.
---
 src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs b/src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs
index 0bc62db..c65bf04 100644
--- a/src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs
+++ b/src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs
@@ -1097,7 +1097,23 @@ fn distribute_item_space_to_base_size(
             &track_limit,
         );

-        // 3. Distribute remaining span beyond limits (if any)
+        // 3. Distribute space to non-affected tracks: space left once the affected tracks reach
+        // their limits goes to the item's other spanned tracks, up to their own limits
+        // (css-grid-2 §12.5.1, w3c/csswg-drafts#3648).
+        let extra_space = if extra_space > THRESHOLD {
+            distribute_space_up_to_limits(
+                extra_space,
+                tracks,
+                |track| !track_is_affected(track),
+                |_| 1.0,
+                get_base_size,
+                |track| track.fit_content_limited_growth_limit(),
+            )
+        } else {
+            extra_space
+        };
+
+        // 4. Distribute remaining span beyond limits (if any)
         if extra_space > THRESHOLD {
             // When accommodating minimum contributions or accommodating min-content contributions:
             //   - any affected track that happens to also have an intrinsic max track sizing function;
@@ -1132,7 +1148,7 @@ fn distribute_item_space_to_base_size(
             );
         }

-        // 4. For each affected track, if the track’s item-incurred increase is larger than the track’s planned increase
+        // 5. For each affected track, if the track’s item-incurred increase is larger than the track’s planned increase
         // set the track’s planned increase to that value.
         for track in tracks.iter_mut() {
             if track.item_incurred_increase > track.base_size_planned_increase {
